    'How to Use Verbal Signals of Agreement and Understanding\n' +
    'You can also keep up your end of the conversation by giving verbal signals that you are engaged in what is being said. You do this with occasional short interjections that don’t interrupt the employer’s flow but let him know you are paying attention. Comments like “uh-huh,” “that’s interesting,” “okay,” “great,” and “yes, yes,” are verbal equivalents of the body language techniques we’ll discuss further on.\n' +
    'Practical Considerations of Using the Telephone\n' +
