{
  index: 156,
  page: 157,
  text: 'What is your greatest strength?\n' +
    'First talk about a must-have technical skill. For example, a sales professional might talk about prospecting for new clients, illustrating the answer with the tactics and strategies used. Second, talk about one or more of the transferable skills that help you execute this critical part of your job; for example, you could talk about the roles that communication, critical thinking, and multitasking skills play in helping you execute your "greatest strength." This way you give a complete and believable answer that also speaks to skills you apply in other aspects of your work.\n' +
    'What is your greatest weakness?\n' +
    `This is one of the toughest of all interview questions, and often comes right after you have been tossed that softball, "What's your greatest strength?"\n` +
