  text: 'Have you ever had any financial difficulties?\n' +
    'A common question, especially if you deal with money. Tell the truth because when references are checked, salary and credit are at the top of the list. Your answer succinctly gives the circumstances, the facts of your difficulties, and where you stand today in resolving those issues. Do not bring up financial problems until this question is asked or an offer is on the table and references are to be checked.\n' +
    'For someone to check your credit history, he must have your written consent. This is required under the 1972 Fair Credit and Reporting Act. Invariably, when you fill out a job application form, sign it, and date it, you’ve also signed a release permitting the employer to check your credit history.\n' +
