  page: 222,
  text: 'Be careful not to criticize a manager, or you might be seen as a potential management problem. It is safest to say that you didn’t have any of these problems. If there was an unhappy work environment and this opinion was shared by many, you can mention it, but remain nonspecific, although you might say that some people didn’t seem to care about anything they did, and you found this difficult.\n' +
    'Another option: “I didn’t like the way some people gave lip service to the ‘customer comes first’ mantra, but really didn’t go out of their way to keep the customer satisfied. I don’t think it was a fault of management, just a general malaise that seemed to affect a lot of people.”\n' +
    'What do you feel is a satisfactory attendance record?\n' +
